# 7. Update — 2026-08-07 (afternoon): Operational Sweep

## 7.1 rtorrent-mcp — container FIXED (was "unhealthy" for 26h+)

Root cause was never rtorrent: the image's healthcheck sent a bodyless `GET /RPC2`, which rtorrent's SCGI rejects (nginx 502 "upstream prematurely closed connection"). Real XMLRPC **POSTs always returned 200** — the MCP path (`localhost:12224/RPC2`) was functional the whole time.

- Fix: `docker-compose.yml` healthcheck now POSTs a minimal `system.client_version` XMLRPC call → container **healthy**, verified end-to-end
- Data dirs relocated from the dead `qbt-mcp` path to `rtorrent-mcp/{config,watch,logs}` (root cause of the old mount: compose was originally run from the `qbt-mcp` dir with relative `./config` paths); `.gitignore` hardened (`/watch/`)
- Commits: `7d8a66f` (healthcheck fix), `1a6c63c` (gitignore); root cause documented in `docs/RTORRENT_SCGI_FIX_PLAN.md`
- Notes learned: rtorrent rc files must stay LF (CRLF → "Junk at end of input"); user rc at `/data/rtorrent/.rtorrent.rc` is loaded via HOME

